{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfF6gABjrWHH5ous1AYRA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Wn58XTHDDvJszHjJnsBkLp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='attavo/drive.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''    positional = [a for a in argv if a not in (\"--until-ready\", \"--recover\")]\n''','''    report = \"--report\" in argv\n    positional = [a for a in argv if a not in (\"--until-ready\", \"--recover\", \"--report\")]\n''',1)\nold='''    if recover:\n        return _drive_recover(root, m, item_id)\n'''\nnew='''    if report:\n        if until_ready or recover:\n            print(\"attavo drive: --report reads and does nothing else; drop --until-ready \"\n                  \"and --recover\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n        from attavo.report import drive_report\n        print(json.dumps(drive_report(root, m, item_id), indent=2))\n        return 0\n\n    if recover:\n        return _drive_recover(root, m, item_id)\n'''\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new,1)\ns=s.replace(\"import io\\nimport os\\n\",\"import io\\nimport json\\nimport os\\n\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='attavo/cli.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"    attavo drive [N] [--until-ready]\\n\",\"    attavo drive [N] [--until-ready | --report]\\n\",1)\nold='''drive is unchanged: one step, then stop, exactly as before.\n'''\nnew='''drive is unchanged: one step, then stop, exactly as before.\n\n--report (reconciler R1) prints, as JSON against schema/drive-report.schema.json,\nwhat item N is waiting on: its state, whose move it is (yours, waits, acts,\ndone), and one sentence in the operator's words. It reads what drive reads --\nthe item's records, its invocation markers, one read of the forge -- and does\nnothing else: it writes no record, starts nothing, terminates nothing, and\ndoes not poll, so a concluded red check reads as blocked-on-checks for as long\nas it is red. It exits 0 on