{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfF74yA7ZM4wvewgPGQQp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016CuKkMJFw6M1AVaEd3GgeX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add attavo/report.py attavo/drive.py attavo/types.py attavo/cli.py schema/drive-report.schema.json tests/test_report.py tests/test_types_mirror_schemas.py tests/test_cli_help.py && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\ndrive --report: what an item is waiting on, and whose move it is (#206)\n\n`attavo drive N --report` prints the item's state, kind (yours, waits,\nacts, done), and one sentence in the operator's words, as JSON against\nschema/drive-report.schema.json. It is drive's own decision read without\nacting on it: drive_state over the records, the invocation readers recovery\nuses, merge_introducing_records for a merged item, and one\nread_forge_checks. It writes nothing, starts nothing, terminates nothing,\nand never polls, so a concluded red check reads blocked-on-checks for as\nlong as it is red (#171).\n\nThe recover path's classification of a marker with no record (running,\nhung, died) moves into drive.read_invocation so recovery and the report\ncannot disagree. attavo drive without the flag behaves as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit status --short; git log --oneline | head -2","description":"Commit the work"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":271,"cache_read_input_tokens":93405,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":271},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8de61c42-af71-4210-8ec4-d6e4cd3c023f","uuid":"97993e09-18b0-46fc-8ffe-c444026732ea","timestamp":"2026-09-20T17:43:24.846Z